"type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Johanna:</strong> Hey, Martin. Do you know anything about data types? I don't understand that topic, and I am taking an exam next Monday. Do you have some time?<br/>\n<strong>Martin:</strong> Actually, I am not doing anything right now. I can briefly explain to you what data types are. However, if you want to pass your exam, you must study hard this weekend. My explanation is not going to be enough.<br/>\n<strong>Johanna:</strong> Yeah, I know. I have to pass this exam or I am failing the course. I am not going out this weekend; I am staying home and studying. So, what exactly are data types?", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "33000", "text": "<strong>Martin:</strong> To begin, you must remember that data is just a series of bits in memory locations located in a circuitry of a computer. However, data types depend on the programming language that you, as a programmer, are using. Data types are very similar from language to language, but there are certain variations. The language normally specifies the kind of values for a determined data type. It also states how the computer processes and stores these values.<br/>\n<strong>Johanna:</strong> That is very interesting. How about some examples of data types?", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "70000", "text": "<strong>Martin:</strong> I can mention a few off the top of my head. Let's see. First, there are integers, which are whole numbers without fractional parts. Then, we have floating point numbers or floats, which are numbers that can contain a fractional part. Next, we find characters, which can be letters and symbols different from numbers. Finally, there are strings, which can be a combination of alphanumeric symbols. There are many others, but you have to study them by yourself. <br/>\n<strong>Johanna:</strong> Thank you, Martin. You are very helpful. Sure, I am studying the whole weekend. I have to apply myself if I want to graduate.", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le02ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}